Cook - E-comOS Package Manager
=======================================
Welcome!
LadinOS was an nascent Linux distribution that nearly failed.Developed and released by the LadinOS Operation Team, and still in pre-release status, it was actually created as preparation for the E-comOS operating system project. We learned a lot from its failure, one of the most valuable lessons being the ALS package manager.
Users of any operating system need to download software; relying solely on the system's built-in software to complete tasks is simply wishful thinking.
So how exactly do users download software? Should we learn from Windows? Their (Microsoft's) "foolproof installers" are indeed appealing, but they're confusing—should we use modern UWP or Win32—which is an EXE file, of course? And why is there an installer format called EXE and another called MSI? Besides, EXE wasn't originally intended for installers! What's the difference between EXE and MSI? I might just want to install Visual Studio.
Instead of creating this mess, we should directly learn Linux's package management system. It's simpler, faster, and more secure, as packages are officially or community certified and generally won't cause major problems.
As we said, we need to develop our own package manager. Is it difficult? No, in modern times, there are many ways to achieve this.
Cook is the foundation for RUI MALL's operation and system updates. Therefore, under normal circumstances, as a core user-space component, it is neither allowed nor permitted to be deleted. If you want to switch to a different package manager, well... it seems there really isn't a replacement (of course, you can fork this repository and modify it a bit).
Let's get down to business.
=======================================
How to use
=======================================
Cook referenced the designs of DNF and APT, creating a set of very simple, fast, and easy-to-remember commands:
Usage: cook <command> [options] [arguments]
Package Management Commands:
  install <package...>          Install one or more packages
  uninstall <package...>        Uninstall one or more packages
  update <package...>           Update specified packages to latest version
  upgrade                       Upgrade all installed packages
  upgrade-full                  Perform a full system upgrade
  hold <package...>             Prevent packages from being upgraded
  unhold <package...>           Allow packages to be upgraded again
  search <query>                Search for packages in repositories
  info <package>                Show detailed information about a package
  list                          List all available packages
  pkg-status <package>          Show installation status of a package
  update-list                   Update package source list
  
Repository Management Commands:
  update-list                   Update local package index from repositories
  add-remote <name> <url>       Add a new remote repository
  rm-remote <name>              Remove an existing remote repository

System Management Commands:
  fuck                          Rollback system to previous version (or specified version)
  status                        Show overall system and cook status
  upgrade-system                Upgrade operating system components

Utility Commands:
  help [command]                Show this help message or help for a specific command
  version                       Show cook version information
    
